      "writtenOn": "2023-11-23T00:59:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "delete this. Reasons:\n\ncopy_file.out expects a path not a label:\n\nhttps://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel-skylib/blob/main/docs/copy_file_doc.md\n\nSo you should have `_KUNIT_DIR + \"/\" + m` here.\n\nnit: also consider using paths.join:\n\nhttps://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel-skylib/blob/main/docs/paths_doc.md\n\nEven if you need a label, this package is not necessarily named //common. Using relative labels helps relocation in the future.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 691,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 691,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "3358388889fe96e3d753a0c89fa508dc187e03a1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e0659575_e92209de",
        "filename": "BUILD.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 691,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942600
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-23T02:14:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, I had meant to remove //common. `paths.join` makes sense, I didn\u0027t know it was something available.\n\nIf this wasn\u0027t a path situation, is there a reason to prefer `_KUNIT_DIR + \"/\" + m` over `\"{}/{}\".format(_KUNIT_DIR, m)`?",
      "parentUuid": "95104609_5b31eec8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 691,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 691,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "3358388889fe96e3d753a0c89fa508dc187e03a1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
